As we add more and more message types, the request/response type check function needs to go through more and more comparisons. I wonder if we should organize bits to simplify it. E.g., we can have the lowest 8 bits representing the message type, and then the next 8 bits serve as flags. And have a kIsRequestMask=0x10 mask. In this case SCRIPT_CALL will be kIsRequestMask | 0, etc. Then the isRequest function can simply be return kIsRequestMask & type_;.



